77.text:
 Rooms use lib.mkDefault for sub-module enables — you can opt out of anything: {
  cattery = {
    room.desktop.dev.enable = true;
    # Override room defaults:
    cli-apps.dev-kit.javascript.enable = false;  # I use bun standalone
    desktop.hyprland.enable = false;              # I prefer Niri
    desktop.niri.enable = true;
  };
}

78.text:
 Many modules use cattery.user for defaults (git identity, email, GPG, shell): {
  cattery.user = {
    name = "alice";
    email = {
      address = "alice@example.com";
      userName = "Alice";
    };
    defaultUserShell = "fish";  # auto-enables fish module
    gpg.signKey = "ABCD1234";
  };
}

81.text:
 Rooms are available for NixOS, home-manager, and nix-darwin. Each room auto-enables its dependency chain — enable desktop.dev and you get all of basis → general → desktop.basis → desktop.general → desktop.dev. All sub-module enables use lib.mkDefault, so you can override any individual module: cattery.room.desktop.dev.enable = true;
# Still get everything except the stuff you opt out of:
cattery.apps.jetbrains.enable = false;
cattery.desktop.plasma.enable = false;

